abstract:
Infancy is a period characterized by a high growth velocity and a high rate of&#13;
physiological development. Nutrition plays a major role in determining health during&#13;
this critical period of life. Moreover, early nutrition has a programming effect on&#13;
health in later life. Early nutrition has been found to be associated with obesity,&#13;
coronary heart disease, neurodevelopmental outcome, cardiovascular and allergic&#13;
diseases in later life. These associations are supported by evidence from&#13;
experimental studies in infants.
